#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:502
msgid "Avoid crossing curled overhangs (Experimental)"
msgstr "Avoid crossing curled overhangs (Experimental)"

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Avoid crossing curled overhangs (Experimental)"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:504
msgid ""
"Plan travel moves such that the extruder avoids areas where the material may "
"be curled up. This is mostly happening on steeper rounded overhangs and may "
"cause a crash with the nozzle. This feature slows down both the print and "
"the G-code generation."
msgstr ""
"Plan travel moves such that the extruder avoids areas where the material may "
"be curled up. This is mostly happening on steeper rounded overhangs and may "
"cause a crash with the nozzle. This feature slows down both the print and "
"the G-code generation."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:511
msgid "Avoid crossing perimeters"
msgstr "Avoid crossing perimeters"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:512
msgid ""
"Optimize travel moves in order to minimize the crossing of perimeters. This "
"is mostly useful with Bowden extruders which suffer from oozing. This "
"feature slows down both the print and the G-code generation."
msgstr ""
"Optimize travel moves in order to minimize the crossing of perimeters. This "
"is mostly useful with Bowden extruders which suffer from oozing. This "
"feature slows down both the print and the G-code generation."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:519
msgid "Avoid crossing perimeters - Max detour length"
msgstr "Avoid crossing perimeters - Max detour length"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:521
msgid ""
"The maximum detour length for avoid crossing perimeters. If the detour is "
"longer than this value, avoid crossing perimeters is not applied for this "
"travel path. Detour length could be specified either as an absolute value or "
"as percentage (for example 50%) of a direct travel path."
msgstr ""
"The maximum detour length for avoid crossing perimeters. If the detour is "
"longer than this value, avoid crossing perimeters is not applied for this "
"travel path. Detour length could be specified either as an absolute value or "
"as percentage (for example 50%) of a direct travel path."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:531
msgid "In object force travel over infill"
msgstr "In object force travel over infill"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:533
msgid ""
"Plan travel moves in object so they preferentially pass over infill regions. "
"Perimeter crossing is allowed. This feature may increase travel length and "
"slicing time."
msgstr ""
"Plan travel moves in object so they preferentially pass over infill regions. "
"Perimeter crossing is allowed. This feature may increase travel length and "
"slicing time."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:539
msgid "In object force travel over infill - Max detour"
msgstr "In object force travel over infill - Max detour"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:541
msgid ""
"Maximum allowed detour percentage for infill-oriented travel compared to the "
"direct path. If set to 0%, the infill-oriented path is always preferred."
msgstr ""
"Maximum allowed detour percentage for infill-oriented travel compared to the "
"direct path. If set to 0%, the infill-oriented path is always preferred."

