#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Fuzzy skin]
msgid ""
"Fuzzy skin\n"
"Did you know that you can create rough fibre-like texture on the sides of "
"your models using the<a>Fuzzy skin</a>feature? You can also use modifiers to "
"apply fuzzy-skin only to a portion of your model."
msgstr ""
"Fuzzy skin\n"
"Did you know that you can create rough fibre-like texture on the sides of "
"your models using the<a>Fuzzy skin</a>feature? You can also use modifiers to "
"apply fuzzy-skin only to a portion of your model."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Shapes gallery]
msgid ""
"Shapes gallery\n"
"Did you know that PrusaSlicer has a Shapes Gallery? You can use the included "
"models as modifiers, negative volumes or as printable objects. Right-click "
"the platter and select<a>Add Shape - Gallery</a>."
msgstr ""
"Shapes gallery\n"
"Did you know that ApiumSlicer has a Shapes Gallery? You can use the included "
"models as modifiers, negative volumes or as printable objects. Right-click "
"the platter and select<a>Add Shape - Gallery</a>."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Arrange settings]
msgid ""
"Arrange settings\n"
"Did you know that you can right-click the<a>Arrange icon</a>to adjust the "
"size of the gap between objects and to allow automatic rotations?"
msgstr ""
"Arrange settings\n"
"Did you know that you can right-click the<a>Arrange icon</a>to adjust the "
"size of the gap between objects and to allow automatic rotations?"

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Negative volume]
msgid ""
"Negative volume\n"
"Did you know that you can subtract one mesh from another using the Negative "
"volume modifier? That way you can, for example, create easily resizable "
"holes directly in PrusaSlicer. Read more in the documentation. (Requires "
"Advanced or Full mode.)"
msgstr ""
"Negative volume\n"
"Did you know that you can subtract one mesh from another using the Negative "
"volume modifier? That way you can, for example, create easily resizable "
"holes directly in ApiumSlicer. Read more in the documentation. (Requires "
"Advanced or Full mode.)"

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Simplify mesh]
msgid ""
"Simplify mesh\n"
"Did you know that you can reduce the number of triangles in a mesh using the "
"Simplify mesh feature? Right-click the model and select Simplify model. Read "
"more in the documentation."
msgstr ""
"Simplify mesh\n"
"Did you know that you can reduce the number of triangles in a mesh using the "
"Simplify mesh feature? Right-click the model and select Simplify model. Read "
"more in the documentation."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Reload from disk]
msgid ""
"Reload from disk\n"
"Did you know that if you created a newer version of your model, you can "
"simply reload it in PrusaSlicer? Right-click the model in the 3D view and "
"choose Reload from disk. Read more in the documentation."
msgstr ""
"Reload from disk\n"
"Did you know that if you created a newer version of your model, you can "
"simply reload it in ApiumSlicer? Right-click the model in the 3D view and "
"choose Reload from disk. Read more in the documentation."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Hiding sidebar]
msgid ""
"Hiding sidebar\n"
"Did you know that you can hide the right sidebar using the shortcut "
"<b>Shift+Tab</b>? You can also enable the icon for this from "
"the<a>Preferences</a>."
msgstr ""
"Hiding sidebar\n"
"Did you know that you can hide the right sidebar using the shortcut "
"<b>Shift+Tab</b>? You can also enable the icon for this from "
"the<a>Preferences</a>."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Perspective camera]
msgid ""
"Perspective camera\n"
"Did you know that you can use the <b>K</b> key to quickly switch between an "
"orthographic and perspective camera?"
msgstr ""
"Perspective camera\n"
"Did you know that you can use the <b>K</b> key to quickly switch between an "
"orthographic and perspective camera?"

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Camera Views]
msgid ""
"Camera Views\n"
"Did you know that you can use the number keys <b>0-6</b> to quickly switch "
"between predefined camera angles?"
msgstr ""
"Camera Views\n"
"Did you know that you can use the number keys <b>0-6</b> to quickly switch "
"between predefined camera angles?"

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Place on face]
msgid ""
"Place on face\n"
"Did you know that you can quickly orient a model so that one of its faces "
"sits on the print bed? Select the<a>Place on face</a>function or press the "
"<b>F</b> key."
msgstr ""
"Place on face\n"
"Did you know that you can quickly orient a model so that one of its faces "
"sits on the print bed? Select the<a>Place on face</a>function or press the "
"<b>F</b> key."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Set number of instances]
msgid ""
"Set number of instances\n"
"Did you know that you can right-click a model and set an exact number of "
"instances instead of copy-pasting it several times?"
msgstr ""
"Set number of instances\n"
"Did you know that you can right-click a model and set an exact number of "
"instances instead of copy-pasting it several times?"

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Combine infill]
msgid ""
"Combine infill\n"
"Did you know that you can print the infill with a higher layer height "
"compared to perimeters to save print time using the setting<a>Combine infill "
"every</a>."
msgstr ""
"Combine infill\n"
"Did you know that you can print the infill with a higher layer height "
"compared to perimeters to save print time using the setting<a>Combine infill "
"every</a>."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Variable layer height]
msgid ""
"Variable layer height\n"
"Did you know that you can print different regions of your model with a "
"different layer height and smooth the transitions between them? Try "
"the<a>Variable layer height tool</a>. (Not available for SLA printers.)"
msgstr ""
"Variable layer height\n"
"Did you know that you can print different regions of your model with a "
"different layer height and smooth the transitions between them? Try "
"the<a>Variable layer height tool</a>. (Not available for SLA printers.)"

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Undo/redo history]
msgid ""
"Undo/redo history\n"
"Did you know that you can right-click the<a>undo/redo arrows</a>to see the "
"history of changes and to undo or redo several actions at once?"
msgstr ""
"Undo/redo history\n"
"Did you know that you can right-click the<a>undo/redo arrows</a>to see the "
"history of changes and to undo or redo several actions at once?"

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Different layer height for each model]
msgid ""
"Different layer height for each model\n"
"Did you know that you can print each model on the plater with a different "
"layer height? Right-click the model in the 3D view, choose Layers and "
"Perimeters and adjust the values in the right panel. Read more in the "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"Different layer height for each model\n"
"Did you know that you can print each model on the plater with a different "
"layer height? Right-click the model in the 3D view, choose Layers and "
"Perimeters and adjust the values in the right panel. Read more in the "
"documentation."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Solid infill threshold area]
msgid ""
"Solid infill threshold area\n"
"Did you know that you can make parts of your model with a small cross-"
"section be filled with solid infill automatically? Set the<a>Solid infill "
"threshold area</a>. (Full mode only.)"
msgstr ""
"Solid infill threshold area\n"
"Did you know that you can make parts of your model with a small cross-"
"section be filled with solid infill automatically? Set the<a>Solid infill "
"threshold area</a>. (Full mode only.)"

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Search functionality]
msgid ""
"Search functionality\n"
"Did you know that you use the<a>Search</a>tool to quickly find a specific "
"PrusaSlicer setting? Or use the familiar shortcut <b>Ctrl+F</b>."
msgstr ""
"Search functionality\n"
"Did you know that you use the<a>Search</a>tool to quickly find a specific "
"ApiumSlicer setting? Or use the familiar shortcut <b>Ctrl+F</b>."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Box selection]
msgid ""
"Box selection\n"
"Did you know that you can do a box selection with Shift+Mouse drag? You can "
"also box-deselect objects with <b>Alt+Mouse drag</b>."
msgstr ""
"Box selection\n"
"Did you know that you can do a box selection with Shift+Mouse drag? You can "
"also box-deselect objects with <b>Alt+Mouse drag</b>."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Zoom on selected objects or all if none
#: selected]
msgid ""
"Zoom on selected objects or on all objects if none selected\n"
"Did you know that you can zoom in on selected objects by pressing the <b>Z</"
"b> key? If none are selected, the camera will zoom on all objects in the "
"scene."
msgstr ""
"Zoom on selected objects or on all objects if none selected\n"
"Did you know that you can zoom in on selected objects by pressing the <b>Z</"
"b> key? If none are selected, the camera will zoom on all objects in the "
"scene."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Printable toggle]
msgid ""
"Printable toggle\n"
"Did you know that you can disable the G-code generation for the selected "
"model without having to move or delete it? Toggle the Printable property of "
"a model from the Right-click context menu."
msgstr ""
"Printable toggle\n"
"Did you know that you can disable the G-code generation for the selected "
"model without having to move or delete it? Toggle the Printable property of "
"a model from the Right-click context menu."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Mirror]
msgid ""
"Mirror\n"
"Did you know that you can mirror the selected model to create a reversed "
"version of it? Right-click the model, select Mirror and pick the mirror axis."
msgstr ""
"Mirror\n"
"Did you know that you can mirror the selected model to create a reversed "
"version of it? Right-click the model, select Mirror and pick the mirror axis."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:PageUp / PageDown quick rotation by 45
#: degrees]
msgid ""
"PageUp / PageDown quick rotation by 45 degrees\n"
"Did you know that you can quickly rotate selected models by 45 degrees "
"around the Z-axis clockwise or counter-clockwise by pressing <b>Page Up</b> "
"or <b>Page Down</b> respectively?"
msgstr ""
"PageUp / PageDown quick rotation by 45 degrees\n"
"Did you know that you can quickly rotate selected models by 45 degrees "
"around the Z-axis clockwise or counter-clockwise by pressing <b>Page Up</b> "
"or <b>Page Down</b> respectively?"

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Load config from G-code]
msgid ""
"Load config from G-code\n"
"Did you know that you can use File-Import-Import Config to load print, "
"filament and printer profiles from an existing G-code file? Similarly, you "
"can use File-Import-Import SL1 / SL1S archive, which also lets you "
"reconstruct 3D models from the voxel data."
msgstr ""
"Load config from G-code\n"
"Did you know that you can use File-Import-Import Config to load print, "
"filament and printer profiles from an existing G-code file? Similarly, you "
"can use File-Import-Import SL1 / SL1S archive, which also lets you "
"reconstruct 3D models from the voxel data."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Ironing]
msgid ""
"Ironing\n"
"Did you know that you can smooth top surfaces of prints using Ironing? The "
"nozzle will run a special second infill phase at the same layer to fill in "
"holes and flatten any lifted plastic. Read more in the documentation. "
"(Requires Advanced or Full mode.)"
msgstr ""
"Ironing\n"
"Did you know that you can smooth top surfaces of prints using Ironing? The "
"nozzle will run a special second infill phase at the same layer to fill in "
"holes and flatten any lifted plastic. Read more in the documentation. "
"(Requires Advanced or Full mode.)"

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Paint-on supports]
msgid ""
"Paint-on supports\n"
"Did you know that you can paint directly on the object and select areas, "
"where supports should be enforced or blocked? Try the<a>Paint-on supports</"
"a>feature. (Requires Advanced or Full mode.)"
msgstr ""
"Paint-on supports\n"
"Did you know that you can paint directly on the object and select areas, "
"where supports should be enforced or blocked? Try the<a>Paint-on supports</"
"a>feature. (Requires Advanced or Full mode.)"

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Paint-on seam]
msgid ""
"Paint-on seam\n"
"Did you know that you can paint directly on the object and select where to "
"place the start/endpoint of each perimeter loop? Try the<a>Seam painting</"
"a>feature. (Requires Advanced or Full mode.)"
msgstr ""
"Paint-on seam\n"
"Did you know that you can paint directly on the object and select where to "
"place the start/endpoint of each perimeter loop? Try the<a>Seam painting</"
"a>feature. (Requires Advanced or Full mode.)"

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Insert Pause]
msgid ""
"Insert Pause\n"
"Did you know that you can schedule the print to pause at a specific layer? "
"Right-click the layer slider in the Preview and select Add pause print "
"(M601). This can be used to insert magnets, weights or nuts into your "
"prints. Read more in the documentation."
msgstr ""
"Insert Pause\n"
"Did you know that you can schedule the print to pause at a specific layer? "
"Right-click the layer slider in the Preview and select Add pause print "
"(M601). This can be used to insert magnets, weights or nuts into your "
"prints. Read more in the documentation."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Insert Custom G-code]
msgid ""
"Insert Custom G-code\n"
"Did you know that you can insert a custom G-code at a specific layer? Left-"
"click the layer in the Preview, Right-click the plus icon and select Add "
"custom G-code. With this function you can, for example, create a temperature "
"tower. Read more in the documentation."
msgstr ""
"Insert Custom G-code\n"
"Did you know that you can insert a custom G-code at a specific layer? Left-"
"click the layer in the Preview, Right-click the plus icon and select Add "
"custom G-code. With this function you can, for example, create a temperature "
"tower. Read more in the documentation."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Configuration snapshots]
msgid ""
"Configuration snapshots\n"
"Did you know that you can roll back to a complete backup of all system and "
"user profiles? You can view and move back and forth between snapshots using "
"the Configuration - <a>Configuration snapshots menu</a>."
msgstr ""
"Configuration snapshots\n"
"Did you know that you can roll back to a complete backup of all system and "
"user profiles? You can view and move back and forth between snapshots using "
"the Configuration - <a>Configuration snapshots menu</a>."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Minimum shell thickness]
msgid ""
"Minimum shell thickness\n"
"Did you know that instead of the number of top and bottom layers, you can "
"define the<a>Minimum shell thickness</a>in millimeters? This feature is "
"especially useful when using the variable layer height function."
msgstr ""
"Minimum shell thickness\n"
"Did you know that instead of the number of top and bottom layers, you can "
"define the<a>Minimum shell thickness</a>in millimeters? This feature is "
"especially useful when using the variable layer height function."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Settings in non-modal window]
msgid ""
"Settings in non-modal window\n"
"Did you know that you can open the Settings in a new non-modal window? This "
"means you can have settings open on one screen and the G-code Preview on the "
"other. Go to the<a>Preferences</a>and select Settings in non-modal window."
msgstr ""
"Settings in non-modal window\n"
"Did you know that you can open the Settings in a new non-modal window? This "
"means you can have settings open on one screen and the G-code Preview on the "
"other. Go to the<a>Preferences</a>and select Settings in non-modal window."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Adaptive infills]
msgid ""
"Adaptive infills\n"
"Did you know that you can use the Adaptive cubic and Support cubic infills "
"to decrease the print time and lower the filament consumption? Read more in "
"the documentation."
msgstr ""
"Adaptive infills\n"
"Did you know that you can use the Adaptive cubic and Support cubic infills "
"to decrease the print time and lower the filament consumption? Read more in "
"the documentation."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Lightning infill]
msgid ""
"Lightning infill\n"
"Did you know that you can use the Lightning infill to support only the top "
"surfaces, save a lot of the filament, and decrease the print time? Read more "
"in the documentation."
msgstr ""
"Lightning infill\n"
"Did you know that you can use the Lightning infill to support only the top "
"surfaces, save a lot of the filament, and decrease the print time? Read more "
"in the documentation."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Fullscreen mode]
msgid ""
"Fullscreen mode\n"
"Did you know that you can switch PrusaSlicer to fullscreen mode? Use the "
"<b>F11</b> hotkey."
msgstr ""
"Fullscreen mode\n"
"Did you know that you can switch ApiumSlicer to fullscreen mode? Use the "
"<b>F11</b> hotkey."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Printables integration]
msgid ""
"Printables.com integration\n"
"Did you know that when you are browsing Printables.com, you can send 3D "
"model files to PrusaSlicer with a single click? Learn more in the "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"Printables.com integration\n"
"Did you know that when you are browsing Printables.com, you can send 3D "
"model files to ApiumSlicer with a single click? Learn more in the "
"documentation."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Cut tool]
msgid ""
"Cut tool\n"
"Did you know that you can cut a model at any angle and even create aligning "
"pins with the updated <a>Cut tool</a>? Learn more in the documentation."
msgstr ""
"Cut tool\n"
"Did you know that you can cut a model at any angle and even create aligning "
"pins with the updated <a>Cut tool</a>? Learn more in the documentation."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Measurement tool]
msgid ""
"Measurement tool\n"
"Did you know that you can <a>measure</a> the distances between points, edges "
"and planes, the radius of a hole or the angle between edges or planes? Learn "
"more in the documentation."
msgstr ""
"Measurement tool\n"
"Did you know that you can <a>measure</a> the distances between points, edges "
"and planes, the radius of a hole or the angle between edges or planes? Learn "
"more in the documentation."

#: resources/data/hints.ini: [hint:Text tool]
msgid ""
"Text tool\n"
"Did you know that you can add custom text labels to your models or even use "
"the text as a modifier? Learn more in the documentation."
msgstr ""
"Text tool\n"
"Did you know that you can add custom text labels to your models or even use "
"the text as a modifier? Learn more in the documentation."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "Zoneheater mode"
msgstr "Zoneheater mode"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Zoneheater operation mode.\n"
"Off: no zoneheater commands are emitted.\n"
"Static: a fixed power level (zoneheater_static_power) is set once at the "
"start; the variable tool is disabled.\n"
"Variable: per-layer power is controlled via the variable zoneheater power "
"profile; the static power setting is inactive.\n"
"Adaptive: automatic adaptive heating (uses zoneheater_adaptive_multiplier)."
msgstr ""
"Zoneheater operation mode.\n"
"Off: no zoneheater commands are emitted.\n"
"Static: a fixed power level (zoneheater_static_power) is set once at the "
"start; the variable tool is disabled.\n"
"Variable: per-layer power is controlled via the variable zoneheater power "
"profile; the static power setting is inactive.\n"
"Adaptive: automatic adaptive heating (uses zoneheater_adaptive_multiplier)."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "Off"
msgstr "Off"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "Static"
msgstr "Static"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "Zoneheater static power"
msgstr "Zoneheater static power"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "Heater power in percent when using static mode."
msgstr "Heater power in percent when using static mode."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "Adaptive Heating multiplier"
msgstr "Adaptive Heating multiplier"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "Heater power multiplier (0-200%) when using adaptive mode."
msgstr "Heater power multiplier (0-200%) when using adaptive mode."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "Zoneheater settings"
msgstr "Zoneheater settings"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "Allow Auxiliary Heating"
msgstr "Allow Auxiliary Heating"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Allow the use of the auxiliary heating function. If non-steel build plates "
"are installed, using auxiliary heating may melt and damage the build plate. "
"When in doubt, leave this option disabled."
msgstr ""
"Allow the use of the auxiliary heating function. If non-steel build plates "
"are installed, using auxiliary heating may melt and damage the build plate. "
"When in doubt, leave this option disabled."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "Calculation base"
msgstr "Calculation base"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for external "
"perimeters. If left zero, default extrusion width will be used if set, "
"otherwise 1.125 x nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as percentage "
"(for example 200%), it will be computed over the selected calculation base."
msgstr ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for external "
"perimeters. If left zero, default extrusion width will be used if set, "
"otherwise 1.125 x nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as percentage "
"(for example 200%), it will be computed over the selected calculation base."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to allow a manual extrusion width. If left to "
"zero, Slic3r derives extrusion widths from the nozzle diameter (see the "
"tooltips for perimeter extrusion width, infill extrusion width etc). If "
"expressed as percentage (for example: 230%), it will be computed over the "
"selected calculation base."
msgstr ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to allow a manual extrusion width. If left to "
"zero, Slic3r derives extrusion widths from the nozzle diameter (see the "
"tooltips for perimeter extrusion width, infill extrusion width etc). If "
"expressed as percentage (for example: 230%), it will be computed over the "
"selected calculation base."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for first "
"layer. You can use this to force fatter extrudates for better adhesion. If "
"expressed as percentage (for example 120%) it will be computed over the "
"selected calculation base. If set to zero, it will use the default extrusion "
"width."
msgstr ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for first "
"layer. You can use this to force fatter extrudates for better adhesion. If "
"expressed as percentage (for example 120%) it will be computed over the "
"selected calculation base. If set to zero, it will use the default extrusion "
"width."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for infill. If "
"left zero, default extrusion width will be used if set, otherwise 1.125 x "
"nozzle diameter will be used. You may want to use fatter extrudates to speed "
"up the infill and make your parts stronger. If expressed as percentage (for "
"example 90%) it will be computed over the selected calculation base."
msgstr ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for infill. If "
"left zero, default extrusion width will be used if set, otherwise 1.125 x "
"nozzle diameter will be used. You may want to use fatter extrudates to speed "
"up the infill and make your parts stronger. If expressed as percentage (for "
"example 90%) it will be computed over the selected calculation base."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for bridge "
"infill. If left zero, bridge infill width is derived from bridge flow ratio "
"and nozzle diameter. If expressed as percentage (for example 90%) it will be "
"computed over the selected calculation base."
msgstr ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for bridge "
"infill. If left zero, bridge infill width is derived from bridge flow ratio "
"and nozzle diameter. If expressed as percentage (for example 90%) it will be "
"computed over the selected calculation base."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for perimeters. "
"You may want to use thinner extrudates to get more accurate surfaces. If "
"left zero, default extrusion width will be used if set, otherwise 1.125 x "
"nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as percentage (for example 200%) "
"it will be computed over the selected calculation base."
msgstr ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for perimeters. "
"You may want to use thinner extrudates to get more accurate surfaces. If "
"left zero, default extrusion width will be used if set, otherwise 1.125 x "
"nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as percentage (for example 200%) "
"it will be computed over the selected calculation base."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for infill for "
"solid surfaces. If left zero, default extrusion width will be used if set, "
"otherwise 1.125 x nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as percentage "
"(for example 90%) it will be computed over the selected calculation base."
msgstr ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for infill for "
"solid surfaces. If left zero, default extrusion width will be used if set, "
"otherwise 1.125 x nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as percentage "
"(for example 90%) it will be computed over the selected calculation base."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for support "
"material. If left zero, default extrusion width will be used if set, "
"otherwise nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as percentage (for "
"example 90%) it will be computed over the selected calculation base."
msgstr ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for support "
"material. If left zero, default extrusion width will be used if set, "
"otherwise nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as percentage (for "
"example 90%) it will be computed over the selected calculation base."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for infill for "
"top surfaces. You may want to use thinner extrudates to fill all narrow "
"regions and get a smoother finish. If left zero, default extrusion width "
"will be used if set, otherwise nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as "
"percentage (for example 90%) it will be computed over the selected "
"calculation base."
msgstr ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for infill for "
"top surfaces. You may want to use thinner extrudates to fill all narrow "
"regions and get a smoother finish. If left zero, default extrusion width "
"will be used if set, otherwise nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as "
"percentage (for example 90%) it will be computed over the selected "
"calculation base."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Base for percentage-based default extrusion width calculation. Used only for "
"percentage values."
msgstr ""
"Base for percentage-based default extrusion width calculation. Used only for "
"percentage values."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Base for percentage-based first layer extrusion width calculation. Used only "
"for percentage values."
msgstr ""
"Base for percentage-based first layer extrusion width calculation. Used only "
"for percentage values."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Base for percentage-based perimeter extrusion width calculation. Used only "
"for percentage values."
msgstr ""
"Base for percentage-based perimeter extrusion width calculation. Used only "
"for percentage values."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Base for percentage-based external perimeter extrusion width calculation. "
"Used only for percentage values."
msgstr ""
"Base for percentage-based external perimeter extrusion width calculation. "
"Used only for percentage values."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Base for percentage-based infill extrusion width calculation. Used only for "
"percentage values."
msgstr ""
"Base for percentage-based infill extrusion width calculation. Used only for "
"percentage values."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Base for percentage-based bridge infill extrusion width calculation. Used "
"only for percentage values."
msgstr ""
"Base for percentage-based bridge infill extrusion width calculation. Used "
"only for percentage values."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Base for percentage-based solid infill extrusion width calculation. Used "
"only for percentage values."
msgstr ""
"Base for percentage-based solid infill extrusion width calculation. Used "
"only for percentage values."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Base for percentage-based top solid infill extrusion width calculation. Used "
"only for percentage values."
msgstr ""
"Base for percentage-based top solid infill extrusion width calculation. Used "
"only for percentage values."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Base for percentage-based support material extrusion width calculation. Used "
"only for percentage values."
msgstr ""
"Base for percentage-based support material extrusion width calculation. Used "
"only for percentage values."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "Allow excessive extrusion widths"
msgstr "Allow excessive extrusion widths"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Disables the excessive extrusion width safety error for this extruder. The "
"safety error is disabled only if this option is enabled for all extruders. "
"Use with caution."
msgstr ""
"Disables the excessive extrusion width safety error for this extruder. The "
"safety error is disabled only if this option is enabled for all extruders. "
"Use with caution."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "Object first layer extrusion multiplier"
msgstr "Object first layer extrusion multiplier"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "Extrusion Multiplier"
msgstr "Extrusion Multiplier"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Multiplier applied to object extrusions on the first object layer. This does "
"not apply to brim/skirt, support, or raft extrusions. The final extrusion is "
"this multiplier times material extrusion multiplier."
msgstr ""
"Multiplier applied to object extrusions on the first object layer. This does "
"not apply to brim/skirt, support, or raft extrusions. The final extrusion is "
"this multiplier times material extrusion multiplier."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "Object first layer cumulative calculation"
msgstr "Object first layer cumulative calculation"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"If disabled, object extrusions on the first object layer use only Object "
"first layer extrusion multiplier. If enabled, object first layer multiplier "
"is multiplied with the line type multiplier (bridge, perimeter, infill, "
"etc.)."
msgstr ""
"If disabled, object extrusions on the first object layer use only Object "
"first layer extrusion multiplier. If enabled, object first layer multiplier "
"is multiplied with the line type multiplier (bridge, perimeter, infill, "
"etc.)."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "Perimeter extrusion multiplier"
msgstr "Perimeter extrusion multiplier"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid ""
"Multiplier applied to perimeter and gap fill extrusions. External perimeter "
"uses its own multiplier."
msgstr ""
"Multiplier applied to perimeter and gap fill extrusions. External perimeter "
"uses its own multiplier."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "External perimeter extrusion multiplier"
msgstr "External perimeter extrusion multiplier"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
msgid "Multiplier applied to external perimeter extrusions."
msgstr "Multiplier applied to external perimeter extrusions."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
